Privacy Policy — NorSOS
Last updated: 7 October 2026
NorSOS is an emergency assistance application developed by NorthByte Norway Tec Ltd. This Privacy Policy explains how NorSOS accesses, uses, stores, and shares information when you use the application.
1. Information NorSOS Accesses
NorSOS may access the following information:
Location information
NorSOS may request access to your approximate and precise location when you use emergency or location-sharing features. Location access is used to obtain your current coordinates and generate a map link that you may share with trusted emergency contacts.
NorSOS does not continuously track your location and does not intentionally collect location information in the background.
Emergency contact information
You may manually add up to three trusted emergency contacts. Their telephone numbers are stored locally on your device so they can be used when preparing an emergency message.
Application preferences
Settings such as your selected language and location-sharing preference are stored locally on your device.
2. How Information Is Used
Information accessed by NorSOS is used only to provide the application's emergency and safety functions.
This includes:
- obtaining your current location when requested;
- generating a map link containing your coordinates;
- preparing an SMS message for your selected emergency contacts;
- opening the device's telephone application to call the emergency number 112;
- storing your emergency contacts and application preferences locally.
3. Location Sharing
NorSOS does not operate a server that receives or stores your location.
If you choose to share your location, NorSOS creates a Google Maps link based on your current coordinates and prepares a message for your selected trusted contacts.
The message is opened in your device's SMS application. The sending of the message is handled by your device and telecommunications provider.
Your location may therefore be disclosed to the recipients you choose when you send the message.
4. Emergency Calls
NorSOS may open your device's telephone application with the emergency number 112.
NorSOS does not itself operate an emergency service and does not directly handle emergency calls.
Telephone calls are processed by your device, telecommunications provider, and the relevant emergency service.
5. Local Data Storage
NorSOS stores certain information locally on your device, including:
- trusted emergency contact telephone numbers;
- language preference;
- location-sharing preference.
This information is not intentionally uploaded to NorthByte Norway Tec Ltd. servers.
6. Analytics, Advertising and Tracking
NorSOS does not currently use:
- advertising SDKs;
- behavioral advertising;
- analytics services;
- user accounts;
- cloud-based user profiles;
- background location tracking.
NorSOS does not sell personal information.
7. Third-Party Services
Certain NorSOS functions interact with services or applications installed on your device.
These may include:
Google Maps
NorSOS may generate a Google Maps URL containing latitude and longitude coordinates. Opening such a link may result in Google processing information under Google's own privacy policies.
SMS application
NorSOS may open your device's SMS application with a pre-filled emergency message. The SMS provider, device manufacturer, operating system provider, or telecommunications operator may process information independently.
Telephone application and emergency services
Calls initiated through NorSOS are handled by the telephone application, your telecommunications provider, and the relevant emergency authority.
NorSOS does not control the privacy practices of these independent third parties.
8. Data Sharing
NorthByte Norway Tec Ltd. does not intentionally sell, rent, or commercially share NorSOS user information.
Information may leave your device only when you intentionally use functionality such as sending an emergency message, opening a map link, or initiating a telephone call.
Emergency messages may contain your location and are shared with the contacts selected by you.
9. Data Retention
NorSOS does not maintain a remote database of user profiles or emergency contacts.
Information stored locally remains on your device until:
- you modify or remove it;
- application data is cleared;
- or the application is uninstalled.
Location information obtained during an emergency action is used for the relevant operation and is not intentionally retained by NorthByte Norway Tec Ltd. on a remote server.
10. Data Deletion
Because NorSOS does not currently provide user accounts or maintain a cloud-based user database, there is no remote user account to delete.
Users can remove locally stored NorSOS information by changing saved contacts and settings, clearing application data through Android settings, or uninstalling the application.
11. Security
NorSOS is designed to minimize the amount of information handled by the application.
Personal information used by the application's current functionality is primarily processed locally on the user's device.
However, no device, operating system, telecommunications network, or electronic transmission method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.
12. Children
NorSOS is not specifically designed or directed toward children.
The application does not intentionally collect personal information from children through a user account, advertising system, analytics service, or developer-operated backend.
13. Emergency Service Disclaimer
NorSOS is an assistance tool and does not replace official emergency services.
NorSOS cannot guarantee that a telephone call, SMS message, location request, map service, telecommunications service, or emergency response will always be available or successful.
In an emergency, users should follow the instructions and procedures of the appropriate official emergency authorities.
14. Changes to This Privacy Policy
This Privacy Policy may be updated if NorSOS functionality, data practices, legal requirements, or Google Play requirements change.
The latest version will be made available on the official privacy policy webpage.
15. Developer and Contact
Application: NorSOS
Developer: NorthByte Norway Tec Ltd.
Website: https://northbytenorwaytec.se/
Privacy inquiries: [dogukanyegin@northbytenorwaytec.se]
If you have questions concerning this Privacy Policy or the handling of information in NorSOS, please contact us using the privacy contact information above.
